        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-11T15:33:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t the important thing that we don\u0027t collide with an upstream cmdline option? There is a reasonable chance that devices will get a kernel update in the field in the next few years for longer support lifetimes - but they would likely not update the bootloader for fear of bricking the device. So this could force us to support an \"android13_\" cmdline option in an android14 kernel. Wouldn\u0027t be the end of the world but it seems uglier than a more generic android-specific name.",
      "parentUuid": "02a2357a_bc294cc8",
